    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68-a1">

                <pb facs="0123" n="116" xml:id="pg116"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 68.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Commander O’Neil to
                        Mr. Herbert.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Cablegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Limon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-07-10"><hi rendition="#italic">July 10,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>An insurrection has broken out at Bluefields, Nicaragua. Marines and blue jackets
                    on shore at the request of the authorities and the American consul, in order to
                    protect property of American citizens. The authorities of Nicaragua have been
                    overthrown by Mosquito chief. There is less excitement. The situation is
                    improving. I shall withdraw forces within the next few days. The <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi> leaves to-day Bluefields, Nicaragua.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
